```dart
persistConfig = () async {
  await saveCliConfig(home, loadCliConfig(home).copyWith(<live overlays>));
};
```

That renders the freshest on-disk truth on EVERY persist — no hook needed, no mutable `saved`, the whole stale-snapshot class closes with a 1-line change! Cost: one file read+parse persist. persistConfig triggers: mode switch, approval change, skill toggle, models/cube change, `/model`, `/provider` — user-action-frequency, not per-turn. Reading a small yaml file per user action is negligible. 

