{"content":"# Thread: the boot-time `saved` snapshot re-rendered over sanctioned mid-session config edits

Fixed. The save base is no longer frozen at boot: every sanctioned direct write to `~/.fah/config.yaml` now re-syncs the snapshot through a new host hook, so the next persist renders the freshest on-disk truth.

## What landed

- New `AgentCliConfig.onUserConfigFileChanged` hook (`lib/src/cli/agent_cli_config.dart`), fired (awaited) by the settings flows after every successful USER-file direct write:
  - `_upsertConfigYaml` global-scope wins (`lib/src/cli/settings_flow.dart:2394`) — covers the global compaction pick (case 3), harness-mode/context-cap writes, provider timeouts, images, memory stores, `auto_update: on/off` upserts, model-capability upserts;
  - `_clearContextCap` (`lib/src/cli/settings_flow_context_cap.dart`);
  - `_dropAutoUpdateKey` (`lib/src/cli/settings_flow_auto_update.dart`);
  - `_removeCapabilityYaml` (`lib/src/cli/settings_flow_model_caps.dart`).
- bin wiring (your suggested "cleaner general fix" shape): `saved` is now mutable and the hook is `saved = loadCliConfig(home)` (`bin/fah_runapp.dart:1497`), with a `ConfigException` guard that keeps the previous snapshot — an unparseable file still makes the next save refuse loudly through `saveCliConfig`'s own merge-step parse, same as before. Project-scope upserts don't fire the hook (they touch the project file; the snapshot tracks the user file only).
- Case 1 turned out to have a second bug sharing its root: `_clearContextCap` dropped the **whole `agent:` block**, so on this branch (where `agent.mode`/`agent.misuseBreaker` now persist) clearing the cap also deleted those siblings. It now does a surgical `removeYamlPath(source, ['agent', 'contextWindowCap'])` — only the cap key goes, the whole block only when the cap was its last member. Pinned by `test/cli/settings_flow_test.dart` "AC2: clearing the cap keeps the sibling agent keys (gh-1572)"; the pre-existing one-key AC2 behavior is unchanged.
- The provider/model triple, `mode`/`approvalMode`/`allowedTools` and the other live overlays still ride the same `saved.copyWith(<overlays>)` base — nothing about the ticket's headline fix changed shape.

## Regression tests (red first, all four failed on the rework head exactly as your repro described)

`test/cli/config_section_preservation_reg_test.dart`, group "a sanctioned mid-session write survives the next persist (gh-1572 rework)":

- clear-cap removal not resurrected (cap `256000` came back before the fix; now `null`, siblings intact);
- `auto_update: false` drop not resurrected (came back `off` before; now `notify`);
- global compaction pick not overwritten by the non-default boot value (`classic` came back before; now `structured` survives);
- end-to-end through the REAL flow: `startAutoUpdateFlow` drop → hook re-sync → boot-shaped `saveCliConfig` → drop survives, plus a hook-firing pin for both write branches (drop and shared-upsert path).
