{"content":"# Thread: the two regression classes this PR opens have no pinning tests

Both pinning tests are in now — each was written first and failed on the rework head (outputs captured in the rework run), then went green with the fix.

## 1. "A sanctioned mid-session file edit survives the next persist"

`test/cli/config_section_preservation_reg_test.dart`, group "a sanctioned mid-session write survives the next persist (gh-1572 rework)" — 6 tests:

- the inverse invariant is pinned for all three scenarios from the review: clear-cap removal (was resurrected as `256000`), `auto_update: false` key drop (was resurrected as `off`), global compaction pick vs a non-default boot value (`structured` was overwritten by `classic`);
- the write shape is the flows' own: the tests land the edit with the same `removeYamlPath` / `upsertYamlPath` + validate-then-write the flows use, then run the boot-shaped `saved.copyWith(<overlays>)` save;
- the re-sync itself is pinned twice: end-to-end through the REAL `startAutoUpdateFlow` with the hook wired like `bin/fah_runapp.dart` (drop survives the persist because the flow re-synced the snapshot), and a hook-firing count pin for both auto-update write branches;
- the sibling-key half of the clear-cap fix is pinned in `test/cli/settings_flow_test.dart` ("AC2: clearing the cap keeps the sibling agent keys (gh-1572)").

## 2. "Everything the emitter renders passes validateAgentSection"

`test/config/config_service_test.dart`, "pins against cli_config.dart" group:

- "everything the agent emitter renders passes the strict mirror validator" — the mechanical emitter↔validator parity pin (every `_agentSectionYaml` shape → `toYaml()` → `validateAgentSection` must return normally). This failed on the rework head (`unknown "agent" key: misuseBreaker`), proving the drift class you named;
- plus per-key agreement tests for `misuseBreaker` and `stuckTool` (bad value throws from BOTH the boot parser and the mirror; good value parses identically), extending the existing mirror-pin group exactly as suggested.

Also while pinning the backstop I found `providersQueue:` was the one known top-level key still missing from `_diskPreservedSections` (no `CliConfig` field, so the emitter can never render it — a save silently deleted the user's queue, the same leak class as the ticket). It's added, with its own survival test in the same reg file.
